# The Airbus A320's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/a320.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 68% and 92% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# the elevators from 1.6 m out to 5.6 m, hinged three tenths of the
# chord forward of the trailing edge;
# the rudder from 3.2 m above the origin to 7.8 m,
# hinged three tenths of the chord forward of the trailing edge.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing -1.87..0.66 at 12.16 m, -3.11..-1.58 at 16.45 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  -1.239 -12.161 -0.701  -2.727 -16.454 -1.143  0.000 0.746 0.235
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  down  -1.239 12.161 -0.701  -2.727 16.454 -1.143  0.000 0.746 0.235
# tail -16.86..-10.26 at 1.60 m, -17.77..-16.22 at 5.60 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -14.882 -1.600 -1.423  -17.303 -5.600 -2.225  0.000 2.300 0.489
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -14.882 1.600 -1.423  -17.303 5.600 -2.225  0.000 2.300 0.489
# fin -16.63..-11.31 at -3.20 m, -17.74..-15.40 at -7.80 m
surface rudder          fcs/rudder-pos-rad         right -15.038 0.002 -3.200  -17.040 0.001 -7.800  0.000 1.856 0.397
